      <div type="clause" n="23">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 23</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ne beo ænig man æniges teames wyrðe, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.1"/> he getrywe witnesse hæbbe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.2"/>, hwanan him come þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> him man æt befehþ.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne beo ænig man æniges teames wyrþe, buton he habbe treowe gewitnysse, hwanon him cóme þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> him mon æt befehð.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>And ne beo ænig man æniges teames wyrþe, buton he getrywe wittenesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.1-2"/> habbe, hwanan him come þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> him man æt befehþ.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Et non sit quisquam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.3-2"/> alicuius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.4-2"/> aduocationis dignus, nisi credibile testimonium habeat, unde uenerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.5"/> ei quod cum eo deprehenditur.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Si latrocinium inuenitur in manu uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.3-3"/> in potestate alicuius, qui se non poterit excusare, si uult warantem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.4-3"/> nominare, nullo modo ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_23.lnote.oe.5-2"/> liceat, nisi habeat duos idoneos testes, qui fuerint uidentes et audientes, unde sibi uenit quod in manu sua uel in potestate captum est.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Neque quisquam ulla aduocacione tutacionis dignus sit, nisi habeat fidelem testem, unde hoc sibi contigit quod apud illum deprehenditur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="23" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="186" ed="#robertson"/>Ne beo ænig man æniges teames wyrþe, buton he habbe treowe gewitnysse<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_23.robnote.fn.1"/> hwanon him cóme þæt him mon æt befehð.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="266" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ne beo ænig man æniges teames wyrðe butan he getrywe witnesse hæbbe, hwanan him come þæt him man æt befehþ.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>Und niemand sei [im Anefang verklagt,] zu einem Gewährzug<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_23.lnote.de.1"/> berechtigt, wenn er nicht glaubwürdige Zeugenschaft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_23.lnote.de.2"/> hat, woher ihm das [Werthstück] zugekommen sei, welches bei ihm im Anefang angeschlagen wird.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let no one [sued by attachment] be entitled to any vouching to warranty unless he has trustworthy witness as to where what is attached in his possession came to him from.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="187" ed="#robertson"/>And no man shall be entitled to vouch to warranty<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_23.robnote.n.1"/>, unless he has trustworthy witnesses [to declare] whence he acquired the stock which is attached in his possession.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="465" ed="#whitelock"/>And no man is to be entitled to vouch to warranty unless he has trustworthy witness as to where he obtained what is being attached.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="267" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And no one shall be entitled to vouch to warranty unless he has reliable witnesses to the manner by which he came by the goods in his possession.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="326"><ref target="clause:IIAtr_8">II Atr 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">*Vgl. II Atr. 8</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:IEw_1-2">I Ew 1.2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 23: (I Ew 1:2)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="361"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:IEw_1-2">I Ew 1.2</ref> <quote>their subject is covered by II Cn 23 – 24, itself based on ?I Ew 1:2, II As 10, 12, ?III Em 5</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="361"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_10">II As 10</ref> <quote>their subject is covered by II Cn 23 – 24, itself based on ?I Ew 1:2, II As 10, 12, ?III Em 5</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="361"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_12">II As 12</ref> <quote>their subject is covered by II Cn 23 – 24, itself based on ?I Ew 1:2, II As 10, 12, ?III Em 5</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="361"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEm_5">III Em 5</ref> <quote>their subject is covered by II Cn 23 – 24, itself based on ?I Ew 1:2, II As 10, 12, ?III Em 5</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="361"><label>covers same subject</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_3">I Atr 3–3.1</ref> <quote>The ignored clauses are I Atr 3 – 3:1; their subject is covered by II Cn 23 – 24</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II Atr 8.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 327, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">getrywe: omitted B</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">vouch to warranty: That is, swearing to the legal possession of goods.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">illa <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">illa Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">contingit <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">contingit Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aliquis <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aliquis K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aliqua aduocacione <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aliqua aduocacione K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ipsi u. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ipsi u. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">habbe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">habbe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">al. uel in p. <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">al. uel in p. Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">guar. <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">guar. S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anefang 12.—Im Ausdruck ähnlich <hi rend="italic">cenne se, þe he hit æt befó, hwanon hit him come</hi> II Atr 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anefang 12.—Similar in expression is <hi rend="italic">cenne se, þe he hit æt befó, hwanon hit him come</hi> II Atr 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_23.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zwei Kaufzeugen (<hi rend="italic">s. d</hi>. 6) Inst, ohne sonstigen Beleg, vielleicht willkürlich aus Kanonistik, gegen <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 24</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Two witnesses of purchase (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word, 6) Inst, with no other instance, perhaps arbitrarily from canon law, contrary to <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 24</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_23.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. I Edw. 1, 1 ff.; I Edg. 4, 1; II Atr. 8</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_23.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><label>gewitnysse</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">getrywe witnesse</hi> (<hi rend="italic">wittenesse</hi>) G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
